                    "tab_title": "What is a Badri cow?",
                    "tab_content": "The Badri cow is an indigenous hill breed native to the Uttarakhand Himalayas — one of India's 50 recognised indigenous cattle breeds (NBAGR). Badri cows graze on Himalayan alpine herbs, giving their milk and ghee a distinctive richness.",
                    "_id": "0596efc2"
                  },
                  {
                    "tab_title": "Is Badri ghee different from regular A2 ghee?",
                    "tab_content": "Yes. While all Badri cow ghee is A2, it comes from a specific indigenous Himalayan breed. The diet — Himalayan herbs, clean mountain water, natural grazing — makes it rare. Think single-origin coffee vs. a blend.",
